# Project map (Godot 4.x)

- **Combat orchestrator:** `combat/CombatManager.gd` — Node with `combatants`, `event_queue`, signals. Keeps registration, `start()`, and thin `func` forwards. Loaded via `core/ResourcePaths.gd` → `COMBAT_MANAGER`.
- **Combat subsystems (preload from manager or call static):** `CombatProcessTick`, `CombatEventScheduler`, `CombatEventDispatch`, `CombatResolveAction`, `CombatEngagementResolver`, `CombatFormationFlow`, `CombatFormationSetup`, `CombatDistanceBands`, `CombatCombatantsSnapshot` (UI rows), `CombatMedicalCoordination` (retry / parts under treatment), `AttackResolver`, `AvailableActionsBuilder`, `MedicalPhaseController`, etc. under `combat/`.
- **Tuning:** `combat/CombatConstants.gd` is large by design (single source of numeric constants).
- **Entities:** `core/CoreEntity.gd` plus `EntityMedical`, `EntityDamage`, `EntityWounds`, …
- **Battle UI:** `ui/BattleScene.gd`, `BattleUIUpdater.gd`, row/diagram builders under `ui/`.

When adding behavior, extend the **smallest** existing module that owns that concern; avoid growing `CombatManager.gd` beyond orchestration and public API.
